                <pb facs="0617" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg605"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.91262/236: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-09T20:00:00-05:00">April 9, 1941—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>955. For Paris. Your 1073, April 7. The Department appreciates the difficulties
                    of the Allen case and has full confidence in your judgment and that you will
                    exhaust every possibility to obtain Allen’s release.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
